```

A constant-radius beam with bRoundCap=false represents a cylindrical mask. Its role here is local repair, not a powder vent. The seam position is provided by the task, and the result remains a candidate until the repaired transition is checked. Curless and Levoy (1996), https://doi.org/10.1145/237170.237269, supports visibility-aware volumetric range integration, not inferring a solid from arbitrary unoriented points. Here the selected loader states its input assumptions, and the repair operates on its resulting voxel field. Positive Offset dilates; negative Offset erodes. Neither morphology nor voxel-to-mesh conversion establishes scan accuracy, manifoldness, support freedom, or manufacturing authorization. The final geometry must pass the reported wall, overhang, connected-void, and powder-route screens before process review.

The program preserves screened nonempty candidates with a pass or rejection report; invalid input and impossible construction assumptions fail before export. Topology and wall screens are finite-resolution evidence; a watertight mesh does not establish metrological accuracy. Minimum wall thickness does not resolve residual stress (Mercelis & Kruth 2006, DOI:10.1108/13552540610707013). Materialise powder-removal dimensions are service-specific; check clearance and actual extraction on the chosen process.

Run in a new empty output directory. The program requires a project targeting net9.0 with PicoGK 2.3.0 and the matching native runtime. Core types are Mesh and IImplicit; this version has no PolyMesh/VoxelMatrix or Voxels.Sub API.

