A dilation of the original field bounds permitted repair additions. Intersecting with that field limits the spatial reach of the repair, although the bound does not guarantee the inserted material represents an actual surface. Curless and Levoy (1996), https://doi.org/10.1145/237170.237269, supports visibility-aware volumetric range integration, not inferring a solid from arbitrary unoriented points. Here the selected loader states its input assumptions, and the repair operates on its resulting voxel field. Positive Offset dilates; negative Offset erodes. Neither morphology nor voxel-to-mesh conversion establishes scan accuracy, manifoldness, support freedom, or manufacturing authorization. The final geometry must pass the reported wall, overhang, connected-void, and powder-route screens before process review.

