The nominated core is an explicit occupancy-preservation constraint. Any core loss causes rollback, even when total volume change is small. This does not establish local thickness; it only guarantees the chosen core occupancy is retained by the edit. Curless and Levoy (1996), https://doi.org/10.1145/237170.237269, supports visibility-aware volumetric range integration, not inferring a solid from arbitrary unoriented points. Here the selected loader states its input assumptions, and the repair operates on its resulting voxel field. Positive Offset dilates; negative Offset erodes. Neither morphology nor voxel-to-mesh conversion establishes scan accuracy, manifoldness, support freedom, or manufacturing authorization. The final geometry must pass the reported wall, overhang, connected-void, and powder-route screens before process review.

