public sealed class Tpms(int kind, float cell, int warp, Vector3 centre) : IImplicit
{
    public float fSignedDistance(in Vector3 p)
    {
        Vector3 q = p - centre;
        float k = 2 * MathF.PI / cell, x = k*q.X, y = k*q.Y, z = k*q.Z;
        if (warp == 1)
        {
            // Integrated phase: local axial period a(z)=cell*(1+0.03*z), not k(z)*z.
            float u = 1 + 0.03f*q.Z;
            // The render domain is validated before entering the native callback.
            z = k * MathF.Log(u) / 0.03f;
        }
        if (warp == 2) { x = k*(0.8660254f*q.X + 0.5f*q.Y); y = k*(-0.5f*q.X + 0.8660254f*q.Y); }
        if (warp == 3) z *= 0.65f; // Characterized anisotropic phase; screen the final slopes.
        // von Schnering & Nesper 1991 DOI:10.1007/BF01313411: dimensionless Fourier nodal approximations.
        float f = kind switch {
            0 => MathF.Sin(x)*MathF.Cos(y) + MathF.Sin(y)*MathF.Cos(z) + MathF.Sin(z)*MathF.Cos(x),
            1 => MathF.Cos(z)*MathF.Sin(x+y) + MathF.Sin(z)*MathF.Cos(x-y),
            _ => MathF.Cos(x) + MathF.Cos(y) + MathF.Cos(z) };
        // shortcut: f/k is a zero-set carrier rather than exact SDF, re-distance its mesh before offsets.
        return f / k;
    }
}

public sealed class Box(Vector3 lo, Vector3 hi) : IImplicit
{
    public float fSignedDistance(in Vector3 p)
    {
        Vector3 q = Vector3.Abs(p - (lo + hi) / 2) - (hi - lo) / 2;
        return Vector3.Max(q, Vector3.Zero).Length() + MathF.Min(MathF.Max(q.X, MathF.Max(q.Y, q.Z)), 0);
    }
}
```

Diamond uses the von Schnering–Nesper Fourier nodal approximation, DOI:10.1007/BF01313411. The raw function is dimensionless; Sheet reconstructs distances and uses offsets in mm. Remove a 3 by 3 mm vertical square keepout from the shell and infill together, after union, so no lattice refills the channel. These geometry changes do not implement Sigmund's FE homogenization optimizer (DOI:10.1016/0020-7683(94)90154-6). A standard sheet can fail the >45-degree rule; preserve and reject those cases instead of claiming universal self-support.

The program preserves screened nonempty candidates with a pass or rejection report; invalid input and impossible construction assumptions fail before export. Topology and wall screens are finite-resolution evidence; a watertight mesh does not establish metrological accuracy. Minimum wall thickness does not resolve residual stress (Mercelis & Kruth 2006, DOI:10.1108/13552540610707013). Materialise powder-removal dimensions are service-specific; check clearance and actual extraction on the chosen process.

Run in a new empty output directory. The program requires a project targeting net9.0 with PicoGK 2.3.0 and the matching native runtime. Core types are Mesh and IImplicit; this version has no PolyMesh/VoxelMatrix or Voxels.Sub API.

