Sigmund (1994), DOI:10.1016/0020-7683(94)90154-6, optimizes microstructures using constitutive targets and FE homogenization. This small example only ranks voxel-measured density with a deliberately labelled rho-squared toy modulus. It does not reproduce Sigmund's optimizer or prove improved stiffness. The selected morphology still must pass the independent final geometric screens.

