ScalarField.fSignedDistance ignores bGetValue failure and therefore maps absent data to zero. The occupancy query belongs to Voxels.bIsInside; raw field sampling must retain an availability flag. This separates missing data from actual zero-level samples. Curless and Levoy (1996), https://doi.org/10.1145/237170.237269, supports visibility-aware volumetric range integration, not inferring a solid from arbitrary unoriented points. Here the selected loader states its input assumptions, and the repair operates on its resulting voxel field. Positive Offset dilates; negative Offset erodes. Neither morphology nor voxel-to-mesh conversion establishes scan accuracy, manifoldness, support freedom, or manufacturing authorization. The final geometry must pass the reported wall, overhang, connected-void, and powder-route screens before process review.

The program preserves screened nonempty candidates with a pass or rejection report; invalid input and impossible construction assumptions fail before export. Topology and wall screens are finite-resolution evidence; a watertight mesh does not establish metrological accuracy. Minimum wall thickness does not resolve residual stress (Mercelis & Kruth 2006, DOI:10.1108/13552540610707013). Materialise powder-removal dimensions are service-specific; check clearance and actual extraction on the chosen process.

